      "text": "To assess how single cell spatial information changes in the DG, we mapped the calcium activity traces to the position of the mouse on the treadmill to generate a tuning vector (Fig. 3a, b). The mean calcium signal at each location was computed for every neuron and normalized to the time the mouse spent at that position. The modulus of the tuning vector was used as a spatial tuning index that reflects the place-specificity of activity29."
